The stylesheet in src/styles/ carries the look of MyMonero's web wallet
(https://github.com/mymonero/mymonero-web-js, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c)
2014-2019, MyMonero.com), read at commit b89b7c6 on 2026-09-14.

What is carried over is the design system that stylesheet states by repetition:
the shape of a dark surface ramp and the text ramp above it, the two-part
elevation recipe (a half-pixel inset highlight over a one-pixel dark shadow),
the 13/12/11/10 px type scale with 0.5 px tracking, the fixed 95 px rail, the
24 px status strip, and the label-over-value field row.

The ramp's values are no longer MyMonero's. It was that stylesheet's
(#161416, #272527, #1d1b1d, #383638, #494749) until 2026-09-17, when the four
Qnero surfaces moved to one palette of their own in `brand/tokens.css`: a warm
neutral ramp of #141312, #262320, #1e1c1a, #322e29 and #2e2b28. The radii were
MyMonero's 3 px and 5 px and are now a single 4 px. What remains derived is the
structure above, not the numbers. No file was copied; src/styles/tokens.css states
those values as custom properties, which the original does not have.

What is not carried over: the accent colour, which is the one value in that
palette that carries MyMonero's identity; the light palette, which is this
project's own; and the `Native-*` typefaces, which are a licensed retail family
outside the BSD grant on the source. The type roles are filled by Archivo and
IBM Plex Mono, both SIL Open Font License 1.1, self-hosted with their licence
text beside them in `src/styles/fonts/`.

The palette itself is no longer stated here: it is `brand/tokens.css`, shared
with the other three Qnero surfaces, and `src/styles/brand-tokens.css` is a
copy of it.

